Here you'll find information about Vcore on Polaris GPUs and its potential problems. 

==The Controller Circuit==
Depending on the card, VCore is controlled by either [https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/pb-ir3567b.pdf?fileId=5546d462533600a4015356803a7228ef IR3567B] (does not have full datasheet available but [https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-IR35201MTRPBF-DS-v01_00-EN.pdf?fileId=5546d462576f347501579c95d19772b5 this one] is close enough), [https://media.digikey.com/pdf/Data%20Sheets/ON%20Semiconductor%20PDFs/NCP81022.pdf NCP81022], or [https://pdf1.alldatasheet.com/datasheet-pdf/view/1113459/UPI/UP9505PQGW.html UP9505P].

Note that all of these controllers have firmware on them, you cannot simply just replace it with a new one if it dies, you either need to flash it yourself or get it from a donor card.

[[VDDCI Rail on Polaris GPUs Explained|VDDCI]] is also created on the VCore controller If the card is using an NCP81022 or UP9505P.

-Schematic is only available for IR3567B variant-
